# Line endings are decided here, not by each machine's core.autocrlf.
#
# Without this file the checked-in generated files (the Flutter plugin
# registrants, the l10n output) sat permanently "modified" in `git status`
# while hashing identically to the index: Git stored them with CRLF, the
# Flutter tooling rewrote them with LF, and neither side was wrong.
#
# Every text file is stored with LF in the repository and checked out with
# LF, which is what the Dart/Flutter toolchain writes and what CI formats
# against. Windows-native files that tooling prefers with CRLF are listed
# below.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Read by Windows tooling (Inno Setup, the resource compiler) and by hand on
# Windows; keep them CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.iss text eol=crlf
*.rc  text eol=crlf

# Never convert these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip binary
*.pdf binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.so binary
*.dylib binary
